# 4data Doctrine

## Non-negotiables
- No persistence in v1
- No replay
- No silent capture
- No inference as fact
- No personalization
- No cross-lane leakage

## Source of truth
- Authoritative signals are real-world deltas only.
- Synthetic/derived output can never be treated as ground truth.

## Lanes and magnets
- Magnets are pure: classify, don’t mutate or store.
- Lanes are isolated: independent TTL, viewport, snapshot rules.
- Cross-lane aggregation must be explicit and auditable.

## Snapshots
- Only exist when explicitly requested.
- Must declare lane, window, intent.
- Discardable immediately; never auto-generated.

## Data factory boundary
- Begins after snapshots, never before.
- Only emits derived, non-replayable products.
- No raw access resale, no identifiers.

## LLM boundary
- LLMs may see aggregates, summaries, context.
- LLMs may never see raw streams, timelines, or authoritative signals.

## Governance
- v1 is frozen (v1.0.0-ephemeral) and enforced by CI.
- Boundaries enforced by ESLint + folder taxonomy.
- Violations fail fast (build/lint), not at review.
